# ROTATIONAL MEDICINE BALL THROW

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Rotational Medicine Ball Throw is an explosive whole-body exercise designed to maximize rotational power through rapid force production and efficient kinetic chain sequencing.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer power exercises for striking-based combat sports.

---

# Philosophy

Combat power is rarely linear.

Punches, elbows, hooks, overhands and many throws rely upon rotational force generated from the ground and transmitted through the hips, trunk and upper limbs.

CAS selects the Rotational Medicine Ball Throw whenever rotational explosiveness is a primary performance objective.

